      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10456374::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC12525669::web::006::1_introduction",
        "PMC12565319::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Alloy modifications that enhance passive-film stability produce faster repassivation after wear.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12525669::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Promoting stable oxide formation can improve resistance to coupled friction and corrosion.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10456374::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Promoting boride formation can enhance passive-film stability.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12565319::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "A mixed FCC/BCC microstructure can constitute a balanced initial state capable of forming a protective passive film.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12525669::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mechanical sliding intermittently removes or disrupts the passive film.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Rapid repassivation shortens the time during which wear-created defects are exposed to the corrosive medium.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12525669::web::006::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The balance between passive-film disruption and repair governs non-additive degradation under simultaneous wear and corrosion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Under combined wear-corrosion conditions, the modified alloy will have a lower overall degradation rate than the baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10456374::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC12565319::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will exhibit lower wear volume than the baseline under combined degradation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10456374::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC12565319::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will exhibit lower corrosion current density than the baseline under combined degradation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC12525669::web::006::1_introduction",
        "PMC12565319::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Effective passivation will reduce both the wear component and the corrosion component of combined degradation.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10456374::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC12565319::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
